---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import DetailHeader from "../../components/DetailHeader.astro";
import DetailPostLayout from "../../layouts/DetailPostLayout.astro";

import sofas_different_mozaic from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/sofas_collage_8k_rotated.webp";
import sofas_mozaic from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/sofas_mozaic.webp";
import sofa_closeup from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/sofa_example_closeup.webp";
import sofa_far from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/sofa_example_far.webp";
import sofa_side from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/sofa_example_side.webp";
import sofa_single from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/sofa_single_mozaic.webp";
import sofa_example2 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/NATUZZIITALIA-ReviveQuiltedQueen_SandChenille_Navy_roomC_Far.webp";
import sofa_example4 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/NONCHALANCE_FERRARA_Velvet_LightGrey_roomB_Far.webp";
import sofa_example8 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/NATUZZIITALIA-ReviveQuiltedQueen_Boucle_MarineBlue_roomB_Far.webp";
import new1 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/new_chair1.webp";
import new2 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/new_chair2.webp";
import new3 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/new_chair3.webp";
import new4 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/new_sofa.webp";
import new5 from "../../assets/projects/Sofas/new_sunbed.webp";

---
<DetailPostLayout
	title="Sofa"
	description = 'Sofa Visualization',
	keywords = 'Sofas, Product Visualization',
>
	<div class="post">
		<main class="post-wrapper">
			<DetailHeader
			tag="PROJECT"
			description="">
					<h1 class="font-type">
						Sofas
					</h1>
			</DetailHeader>

			<section>
				<div class="content">
					<div class="row desc">
						<div class="col-1a">
							<p class="post-desc">
								<p>
								I worked with multiple clients that required high-quality renders for their sofa/chairs collection.
								<br>
								One of the client required multiple variations(materials and colors), with over 7000 images delivered.
								<br>
								Other client was interested in quick prototying to create unique models with different variants to explore different design choices.
								</p>
								<p>
								For large batch of renders I developed a procedural rendering system that made it easy to configure process any combination of models, colors and materials.
								</p>
								<p>
								Some models were created from scratch, based on references, other models started as CAD files, which had to be rebuilt to high-resolution meshes. I have fixed geometry, UVs, added missing details(piping, stitches) and used cloth simulation to give realistic shape to fabrics.
								</p>
								<p>
								An automated scene assembly system handled camera placement and framing, ensuring consistent composition across all variations. The pipeline generated organized, properly named outputs, ready for client review and delivery.
								</p>
								<p>Additionally, I produced an animation sequence showing the transformation from old, worn fabric to new upholstery, highlighting the brand’s craftsmanship and attention to detail. </p>
								<video width="100%" autoplay loop muted >
									<source src="/assets/projects/Sofas/BubbleTransition_v10.mp4" type="video/mp4">
								</video>
								<p>Let's look at few models:
								<Image src={new1} alt="Single chair" />
								<Image src={new2} alt="Single chair" />
								<Image src={new5} alt="Single sunbed" />
								<Image src={new3} alt="Single chair" />
								<Image src={new4} alt="Single sofa" />
								<Image src={sofa_example2} alt="Single Sofa example" />
								<Image src={sofa_far} alt="Single sofa, angled shot" />
								<Image src={sofa_side} alt="Single sofa, side shot" />
								<Image src={sofa_example8} alt="Single Sofa example" />
								<p>Here are all possible variations for single sofa: </p>
								<Image src={sofa_single} alt="Single sofa, multiple views and colors" />						
								<p>Here are sofas with the consistent color and angle:</p>
								<Image src={sofas_mozaic} alt="different sofas with different colors and angles" />
								<p>Here are different models with different colors and angles:</p>
								<Image src={sofas_different_mozaic} alt="different sofas with different colors and angles" />									<p>
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
	</div>
</DetailPostLayout>

<style>
img{
	border:1px solid #ececec;
}
.btn{
	display: flex;
	gap: 16px;
}
</style>
